# The native archive pointer is an engine-owned transient object. Wasm gets
# the lifecycle notification through the safe empty query; archive access must
# use a future scoped VFS/handle ABI rather than exposing the raw pointer.
# LuaUI receives Load, but CLuaHandle::Save explicitly excludes user-mode
# handles, so these two callins intentionally have different UI masks. The
# internal ArchiveCallin entry remains for the shared native function-pointer
# typedef and is never dispatched directly by the engine.
CALLIN(ArchiveCallin, SimpleCallinQuery, ArchiveCallinResult, rules-synced|rules-unsynced|gaia-synced|gaia-unsynced, ignore, archive-notification)
CALLIN(Load, SimpleCallinQuery, ArchiveCallinResult, rules-synced|rules-unsynced|gaia-synced|gaia-unsynced|ui, ignore, archive-notification)
CALLIN(Save, SimpleCallinQuery, ArchiveCallinResult, rules-synced|rules-unsynced|gaia-synced|gaia-unsynced, ignore, archive-notification)
